-## How to read this file
-
-### Classes
-
-Each finding has exactly one class.
-
-| Class | Meaning |
-|---|---|
-| supported | A governing source requires other behavior. A native run through the public command, or a reproduction script that uses only the product and a fixture, shows the violation. |
-| conditional | The verdict depends on an open maintainer question. The entry names the question and says what the finding becomes under each option. The Summary splits them into three groups. Some are defects under the question's provisional answer. Some are decided by a new question that has no provisional answer. The rest are defects only under an alternative. |
-| issue | Observed or code-read behavior worth a maintainer's attention, for which no source states a requirement under the current provisional answers. |
-| suspected | Read from the code and not observed natively. A governing source would be violated if the reading is right. A suspected finding whose verdict also depends on a question stays suspected and names it. |
-| withdrawn or refuted | A governing source documents the behavior as intended, or the evidence contradicts the finding. Kept with the reason. |
-| out of scope | Outside the product surface this review covers. Kept with the reason. |
-
-The scope ledger (`.g5/uplift/ipm-quality-followup/scope-ledger.md`) excludes some features from modeling and native runs, for example update steps (OBS-L5, OBS-L9). A finding in such a feature keeps its class here when an ontology I block governs it. Exclusion from verification is not exclusion from filing.
