-## Withdrawn, refuted and out of scope
-
-- D7, withdrawn: `history details` prints the raw `%Status`. wiki/09 L133 documents it on purpose ("so the ObjectScript stack is visible"). Round 1 disposition R1-ONT-13. Evidence R3 (`RN/20261113T184444Z-cases-hr`).
-- OBS-H9, withdrawn: a global history delete (the `-globally` flag) needs no filter and no confirmation. This is the documented decision `history.delete.global-unfiltered` (`features/history.g5.md:271`) and the `-confirm` help ("Ignored if -globally is passed too"). Together with D2, a filtered global delete can also remove every record, which D2 covers.
-- OBS-H10 (remainder), refuted: the uplift suspected that namespaces without IPM appear in `-globally` output as empty groups. `DisplayQueryResult` writes the namespace header only when a row exists (`General/History.cls:501-515`), so such a namespace prints nothing and `history.read.global` ("Namespaces without IPM add no records", `features/history.g5.md:237`) holds. Archived H10 agrees: only USER-VERIFY was listed and no "IPM is not enabled" line appeared (`RN/20261113T204152Z-stagec`, `find.not.enabled.lines=0`). What remains is an unreachable message (`:496-499`), which violates nothing. The independent review found this.
-- OBS-L15, out of scope: `LoadedResource` rows in IRISTEMP (`Document.cls:186`) survive a rolled-back load. Only the `@API` methods `Validate` and `ReportConflicts` read them and those entry points are excluded in `A/coverage-map.md` section 2. IRISTEMP data is outside the rollback under Q-04's provisional answer and `premises.md` P-10 excludes it.
-- OOS-1, out of scope: a git URL load passes the URL and `-branch` to a shell command without quoting (`Main.cls:2356-2358`). Running it already needs the caller's own OS callout privilege, and command construction is outside this review's load and history scope. This review made a static observation only and did not test it. The maintainers may want to assess it through their security process.
-- OOS-2, out of scope: the module that `verify` installs into the VERIFY namespace gets no history record while its dependencies do (OP-LOAD-28, A3 disagreement 3). `history.actions` excludes lifecycle phase commands and the ontology notes the case under `build.verify`.
-- OOS-3, out of scope: IPM's test summary counted a skipped method as passed. `Test.PM.Integration.DependencyResolution` printed "Methods: 1 total, 1 passed" although its only method was skipped (`RN/20261113T182409Z-suite-verify-DependencyResolution`, brief E-5). `build.test-output` says only that a summary is printed and test reporting is outside this review's scope.
-- Refuted predictions, kept as contrary evidence:
-  - OBS-L6 predicted that the other module's manifest stays after an `update -path` mismatch. S3 refuted it. The path is D16.
-  - OBS-H6 predicted the start-value row after a Terminate. N-P10 refuted it (`%OnClose` runs at a Terminate). The SIGKILL part holds and is D10.
-  - A1 INT-HIST-03 (d) said an abnormally ended record keeps `Finalized=0` and an orphaned IRISTEMP row. C1 and C2 refuted that for a Terminate (D10, D27).
-  - Platform premise N-P10 and sub-claim N-P20C2 were refuted. They shape the D1 direction and are not product findings.
